Original commit body from c73b06b1c73b65fd1927c4606edaecc0c9968990:

ADR-0050 §1 (owner ruling 2026-10-25) names a row's primary boundary by
the MEDIUM data crosses, and a Unix-domain socket's medium is local IPC.
The vocabulary had no IPC-side deferred-crossing value -- net_listen was
the only listen boundary -- so Go's net.ListenUnix and Python's
asyncio.start_unix_server were rowed net_listen and read as network
ingress. Owner ruling 2026-10-26 (WI-gaziv, option a): add ipc_listen
rather than widen net_listen to "any listener".

ipc_listen is net_listen's local-IPC twin and carries its three ADR-0049
clauses: catalog-declarable, deferred_crossing axis, inbound; mints no
taint; disclosed and held out of total_io_edges in its own
ipc_listen_edges count; shadows ipc_recv (DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS), so
a clean ipc_recv verdict over a program with a Unix listener is
qualified, never granted. It is declared last, so first-declared-wins
leaves every existing row's primary boundary alone.

Rows:
* go: net.ListenUnix moved from net_listen; net.ListenUnixgram (ListenUDP's
  Unix twin, previously unrowed) added.
* python: asyncio.start_unix_server moved from net_listen; serve_forever /
  handle_request on socketserver's six Unix server classes (Unix /
  ThreadingUnix / ForkingUnix x Stream / Datagram) added -- TCPServer, their
  twin, is net_listen.
* Stays net_listen: calls that may bind either medium (socket.socket.bind,
  socket.create_server, go net.Listen / ListenPacket with a network
  argument, syscall and x/sys/unix Socket/Bind/Listen) until a call-site
  stamp can tell them apart.
* Not rowed: loop.create_unix_server -- its receiver is the loop
  get_running_loop() returns, which the analyzer leaves untyped
  (python:external:...), so a row could never match; asyncio's
  loop.create_server has no row for the same reason. And the receive half
  of a Python Unix server, asyncio.StreamReader.read*, stays net_recv
  because TCP and Unix streams share it (WI-muful); the description says so.

io-boundaries envelope: ipc_listen_edges on both the BoundaryMap.to_dict
and the cmd_io_boundaries filtered path; IO_BOUNDARIES_SCHEMA_VERSION 2.4 ->
2.5 (additive). docs/concept-axes.md regenerated (docs/schema.json does not
list boundary values; unchanged). ADR-0050 §2's deferred_crossing row and
§3's headline list, spec §9 / §11 vocabulary and disclosure text (the §9
list was also missing navigation_read and host_info_read; it now matches
CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES exactly).

Consumers that branch on the deferred values were enumerated first:
DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS (now keyed for ipc_listen), the disclosed-only
set (derived from the spec), the envelope counts (both paths, gated by
TestTheTwoEnvelopePathsCannotDrift), verify-claims' deferred caveat
(generic over the shadowed boundary -- no edit). Nothing else keys on
the string.

